  "goodToKnow": "Die Inspektion is an inspection and, for cars, a regular service at the garage (Werkstatt), following the manufacturer's schedule. Separately, every car in Germany must pass the Hauptuntersuchung (HU), commonly called TÜV, every two years (after three years for new cars). Inspizieren means to inspect. Der Inspektor is an inspector. Plural: die Inspektionen."
